## Troubleshooting

### 1. Common Issues

**SonarQube MCP Server:**
```bash
# Check if server is running
docker ps | grep sonarqube

# Check environment variables (without exposing secret values)
if [ -z "$SONARQUBE_TOKEN" ]; then
  echo "SONARQUBE_TOKEN is not set"
else
  echo "SONARQUBE_TOKEN is set (length: ${#SONARQUBE_TOKEN} characters)"
fi

if [ -z "$SONARQUBE_ORG" ]; then
  echo "SONARQUBE_ORG is not set"
else
  echo "SONARQUBE_ORG is set to: $SONARQUBE_ORG"
fi
```

**⚠️ SECURITY NOTE**: When troubleshooting in production, avoid echoing sensitive values.
Use validation checks instead of direct echo statements for secrets.

**Coverage Files:**
```bash
# Check coverage files
ls -la coverage/<project>/
ls -la coverage-reports/<project>/

# Regenerate coverage
nx test <project> --coverage
```

**Analysis Failures:**
```bash
# Check project configuration
cat platform/<project>/sonar-project.properties

# Verify dependencies
npm list sonar-scanner
```

### 2. Debug Mode

**Verbose Output:**
```bash
# Enable debug mode
DEBUG=sonarqube nx test <project> --coverage

# Check logs
tail -f coverage-reports/<project>/sonarqube.log
```

### 3. Recovery

**Failed Analysis:**
```bash
# Clean and retry
rm -rf coverage-reports/<project>/
nx test <project> --coverage
```

**Coverage Issues:**
```bash
# Regenerate coverage
rm -rf coverage/<project>/
nx test <project> --coverage
```

